DELIVERY EXPOSURE -- these are physically settled. A short call left in the
money at expiry is an obligation to deliver shares, not a cash debit. Measured
on every entry whose expiry-day bell exists: whether OUR cache quoted the
strike has nothing to do with whether the exchange exercises it.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  median spot at the bell Rs1,262 vs short strike Rs1,280 (gap to long strike Rs20.0)
  spot finishes above the SHORT strike 53.0% of the time
  spot finishes above the LONG strike too 30.4% -- both legs exercise and the deliveries net
  the dangerous band, short ITM with the long expiring worthless: 22.7%
  where the bell lands, in units of the strike gap above the short strike:
      p5      -6.34 gaps
      p25     -1.04 gaps
      p50     +0.12 gaps
      p75     +1.34 gaps
      p95     +5.51 gaps
  squaring off before the bell avoids all of it, by construction.

