SLIPPAGE -- everything above assumes a 5-paise tick crossed on each leg each
way. That is an INDEX-option assumption. Stock options in expiry week are
thinner, and half-crossing a wider quote is where results like this usually
die. Re-priced on the imputed 14:00 exit:
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  half-spread/leg         ROI/risk      win%  Rs/spread    t(day)   openable
  Rs0.05                    -7.96%     50.8%      -1.54     -0.46       100%
  Rs0.25                    -9.48%     46.4%      -1.88     -0.85        97%
  Rs0.50                   -12.90%     39.6%      -2.70     -1.32        94%
  Rs1.00                   -16.74%     34.6%      -4.22     -1.39        77%
  Rs1.50                   -19.15%     31.9%      -5.72     -1.47        64%

  Median credit Rs4.85 against Rs7.20 of risk, so each extra 25 paise of
  half-spread costs Rs1.00 across the four crossings. 'openable' is the share
  of entries still worth a credit at that spread -- the rest simply vanish.

